  "hindi": "हे अग्नि, हमारे मन से स्तुत, योग्य, आज मानुष होता से पहले देवों का यजन करो। वह तुम मरुतों के अविचल गण को यहाँ लाओ; हे नरो, बर्हि पर बैठे इन्द्र का यजन करो।",
  "english": "Invoked with our mind, O Agni, worthy one, worship the gods today, before the human (priest). Bring hither the unshaken host of the Maruts; O men, worship Indra seated on the barhis (sacred grass).",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "saḥ with a 2nd-person imperative (sa ā vaha) is the usual Vedic 'you, that one'. mānuṣāt pūrvaḥ: 'before the human one' (the human hotṛ) is the literal sense; the object of comparison is not stated.",
  "confidence": "high"
 },
