  "hindi": "हे दिव्य बर्हि — बढ़ते हुए, सुवीर, धन के लिए बिछाए हुए, इस वेदी पर सुन्दर भार वाले, घृत से अभ्यंजित इस (बर्हि) पर, हे वसुओ, हे विश्वेदेवो, हे यज्ञ के योग्य आदित्यो, बैठो।",
  "english": "O divine barhis — growing, rich in heroes, strewn for wealth, well-laden on this altar, anointed with ghee: on this sit, O Vasus, all you gods, O Ādityas worthy of sacrifice.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "deva (voc. sg.) is taken with barhiḥ as 'O divine barhis'; the accusatives (vardhamānam ... aktam) then agree with idam (barhiḥ) as the object of sīdata. Alternative: deva as a separate vocative. vedi: endingless locative (padapāṭha-style vedi + asyām).",
